From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:16:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] GSLayoutManager: compile out the glyph run sanity check

-_sanityChecks walks the whole glyph run list to assert its links, and
runs after every incremental glyph generation, so laying out a long text
was quadratic in its runs: a 1.3 MB Markdown document took 125s to lay
out in MarkdownViewer, 0.5s without the walk (danjboyd/ObjcMarkdown#94).
It now runs only when built with GSLAYOUTMANAGER_SANITY_CHECKS defined.

Carried in ObjcMarkdown's Linux packages; not sent upstream.
AI assistance: this change and this description were written with
Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code).
---
 Source/GSLayoutManager.m | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/GSLayoutManager.m b/Source/GSLayoutManager.m
index f6d652c..a1ba0ed 100644
--- a/Source/GSLayoutManager.m
+++ b/Source/GSLayoutManager.m
@@ -318,6 +318,7 @@ Private method used internally by GSLayoutManager for sanity checking.
 
 - (void) _sanityChecks
 {
+#ifdef GSLAYOUTMANAGER_SANITY_CHECKS
   glyph_run_t *g;
 
   g = (glyph_run_t *)&glyphs[SKIP_LIST_DEPTH - 1];
@@ -327,6 +328,7 @@ Private method used internally by GSLayoutManager for sanity checking.
                @"glyph structure corrupted: g->next->prev!=g");
       g = (glyph_run_t *)g->head.next;
     }
+#endif
 }
 
 
